  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
    <body>

        <div xml:id="AN255.1-kilavi">
          <p type="edition">piriviṭai vēṟupaṭṭa talaimaka ḷāṟṟāmai mītūrat tōḻikkuc colliyatu.</p>
          <p type="translation" xml:lang="en">What SHE, who had undergone changes in the time of separation, said to the confidante when [her] lack of strength increased.</p>
        </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="AN255.1">
        <l>ulakukiḷarn taṉṉa vurukeḻu vaṅkam</l>
        <l>pulavuttiraip peruṅka<supplied>ṭa</supplied> ṉīriṭai pōḻa</l>
        <l>viravu mellaiyu macaiviṉ ṟāki</l>
        <l>viraicela liyaṟkai vaṅkū ḻāṭṭak</l>
        <l>kōṭuyar tiṇimaṇa lakaṉṟuṟai nīkāṉ</l>
        <l>māṭa voḷḷeri maruṅkaṟin toyya</l>
        <l>vāḷviṉaip pirinta kātalar nāḷpala</l>
        <l>kaḻiyā maiyē <supplied>ya</supplied>ḻipaṭa rakala </l>
        <l>varuvar maṉṉāṟ ṟōḻi taṇpaṇaip</l>
        <l>porupuṉal vaippi ṉammū rāṅkaṭ</l>
        <l>karuviḷai muraṇiya taṇputaṟ pakaṉṟaip</l>
        <l>peruvaṉa malara valli tīṇṭip</l>
        <l>palavukkāyp puṟatta pacumpaḻap pā<supplied>ka</supplied>l</l>
        <l>kūta<supplied>ḷa</supplied> mūtilaik koṭiniṟai tūṅka</l>
        <l>vaṟaṉiṉ ṟalaikku māṉā vāṭai</l>
        <l>kaṭimaṉai māṭattuk kaṅkul vīcit</l>
        <l><supplied>ti</supplied>runtiḻai ñekiḻntu peruṅkaviṉ cāya</l>
        <l>niraivaḷai yūrun tōḷeṉa</l>
        <l>vuraiyoṭu cellu maṉpiṉarp peṟiṉē.</l>
      </lg>
      <lg type="translation" xml:lang="en">
        <l corresp="1">As the ship, awesome/beautiful like the world emerging [from the sea],</l>
        <l corresp="2">cuts through the water of the vast ocean with fish-reeking waves,</l>
        <l corresp="3">being restless by night and by day,</l>
        <l corresp="4">while the wind drives [it] whose nature is to go fast,</l>
        <l>as the pilot, knowing the [correct] side by the bright flames on storied mansions,</l>
        <l corresp="5f">sends [it] forth into the wide harbour with firm sand high in peaks,</l>
        <l corresp="7a-c">[your] lover who parted [from you] for manly work,</l>
        <l corresp="7d-8">without that many days pass at all, so that [your] desolate affliction departs,</l>
        <l corresp="9a-c">he would surely come, friend,</l>
        <l corresp="19">– if we were to obtain somebody loving who goes [to him] with the word</l>
        <l corresp="18c">that</l>
        <l corresp="9d-10">there in our village, in the region of floods that dash against the cool wet-lands,</l>
        <l corresp="11">while the jalap in cool bushes that contrasts with the mussel-shell creepers</l>
        <l corresp="12">comes into contact with the white lotus with blooms of great beauty</l>
        <l>[and] the fullness of unripe jack fruits [and] balsam pears [still] green</l>
        <l corresp="13f">outside hang down on morning glory creepers with old leaves,</l>
        <l corresp="15">as the unending north wind that, being derelict of duty, harasses [you],</l>
        <l corresp="16">gusts against the storied building, [our] protected house at night,</l>
        <l corresp="17">while the perfect jewels become loose [and] the great beauty is exhausted</l>
        <l rend="indent2" corresp="18">the bangles in a row glide from [your] arms.</l>
      </lg>
        </div>
    </body>
  </text>

